 4. 📚 1 for the road: &quot;First-of-its-kind&quot; library 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Anythink Nature Library in Thornton, Colo. Photo: Unfound Door At a new library just outside Denver, you can get a book, a pair of snowshoes and a trail to use them on, Axios' Alayna Alvarez reports. 

 The Anythink Nature Library includes a 33,000-square-foot library, nature center and community gathering space. The local public library system calls it "the nation's first nature library." 🏕️ The $43.4 million project sits on 15 acres, with a collection that includes wildlife cameras and camping gear alongside books and other nature-focused materials.

 Inside, visitors will find a nature lab, a sunroom, and a darkened space for quiet reflection and sensory learning. An aerial view of the library. Photo: Anythink Nature Library 🥾 Outside, the property features gardens, a trail loop, and a café with indoor and outdoor seating.

 A trailhead connects the library to the 140-acre Aylor Open Lands trail system. Take a look . 

 
 
